# Every path puts the owner on the review, so nothing lands unseen. What keeps
# the core closed is write access, which nobody else has: an outside change
# arrives from a fork and cannot merge itself. Review is not a required check —
# requiring it on a repository with one maintainer only blocks that maintainer,
# and the admin override it forces skips the CI gate along with it.
